24
00:01:43,220 --> 00:01:48,160
So if I've already created an issue under a project in GitLab, I can link to an existing

25
00:01:48,160 --> 00:01:49,160
one.

26
00:01:49,160 --> 00:01:52,080
All I need to do is select project and enter the GitLab issue number.

27
00:01:52,080 --> 00:01:55,200
But in our case, we're just going to create a new issue.

28
00:01:55,200 --> 00:01:59,840
So under the one I've selected earlier, which is the final project, I hit create.

29
00:01:59,840 --> 00:02:04,240
So that has now created a ticket in GitLab.

30
00:02:04,240 --> 00:02:10,140
So if we go to the link tickets tab, we can see that it's loaded a preview of the GitLab

31
00:02:10,140 --> 00:02:11,140
issue here.

32
00:02:11,140 --> 00:02:12,140
So we can see it's issue number two.

33
00:02:12,140 --> 00:02:16,140
We can see a title and we can see the state's currently opened.

34
00:02:16,140 --> 00:02:19,340
So this two here provides a hyperlink directly into GitLab.

35
00:02:19,340 --> 00:02:22,800
So if I go into here.

36
00:02:22,800 --> 00:02:25,900
So this is the issue that's just been created by the BIRP user.

37
00:02:25,900 --> 00:02:29,080
So we'll see a bit of information in here about the issue.

38
00:02:29,080 --> 00:02:32,120
Things like severity, confidence and so on.

39
00:02:32,120 --> 00:02:35,400
And a bit more detail further down.

40
00:02:35,400 --> 00:02:42,140
Also notice that on the right hand side, we've labeled the issue as well.

41
00:02:42,140 --> 00:02:44,300
And towards the bottom.

42
00:02:44,300 --> 00:02:47,740
So the other thing we do is add a comment at the bottom that actually links directly back

43
00:02:47,740 --> 00:02:48,740
to enterprise.

44
00:02:48,740 --> 00:02:53,080
So you can actually click on that and go straight back to the issue in enterprise.

45
00:02:53,080 --> 00:02:55,060
So as we can see, the status is open.

46
00:02:55,060 --> 00:02:57,840
So what I'm going to do is actually close the issue.

47
00:02:57,840 --> 00:02:58,840
Now it's closed.

48
00:02:58,840 --> 00:03:04,160
So if I go back down and head back into enterprise via this link.

49
00:03:04,160 --> 00:03:06,160
Hopefully that should be reflected in here.

50
00:03:06,160 --> 00:03:08,160
So yeah, we can see now the status is closed.

51
00:03:08,160 --> 00:03:11,100
So it's pulled that through from GitLab.

52
00:03:11,100 --> 00:03:15,100
